# recovery/BIN_PARITY_EXEMPT -- targets exempt from the bin-parity byte gate.
#
# `make -C recovery bin-parity` clean-rebuilds every committed
# recovery/bin/<arch>/ artifact with the pinned toolchain (recovery/TOOLCHAIN)
# and SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH and byte-compares it against the committed file.  A
# target listed here is NOT byte-compared -- because its current toolchain
# produces non-byte-reproducible output -- but bin-parity STILL clean-rebuilds
# it (proving it compiles+links) and prints the exemption loudly.
#
# Exemption is a liability, not a free pass: GATE-08 step 5 mandates that each
# exempt target carry a tracking issue.  Drop a target the moment its toolchain
# yields byte-reproducible output (e.g. a future zig with deterministic
# Mach-O/PE linking, or a documented post-link normalization step).
#
# Format (one per line):  <rel-path-under-bin/>  issue=#N  reason="..."
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
# zig 0.16.0's Mach-O linker recomputes LC_UUID + chained-fixup / function-
# starts / code-directory hashes per run (~38KB scattered diff across two
# back-to-back builds); -Wl,-no_uuid is rejected as an unsupported linker arg.
x86_64-macos/lcsas-restore    issue=#320  reason="zig 0.16.0 Mach-O linker non-reproducible"
x86_64-macos/lcsas-keyshare   issue=#320  reason="zig 0.16.0 Mach-O linker non-reproducible"
aarch64-macos/lcsas-restore   issue=#320  reason="zig 0.16.0 Mach-O linker non-reproducible"
aarch64-macos/lcsas-keyshare  issue=#320  reason="zig 0.16.0 Mach-O linker non-reproducible"
# zig 0.16.0's PE-COFF linker embeds a per-run PE header timestamp + debug-
# directory checksum (~20-byte diff across two back-to-back builds).
x86_64-windows/lcsas-restore.exe   issue=#320  reason="zig 0.16.0 PE linker non-reproducible"
x86_64-windows/lcsas-keyshare.exe  issue=#320  reason="zig 0.16.0 PE linker non-reproducible"
